# API host & tenant config

No Android product flavors. Tenant is **runtime** via the login **Server** field. See `mobile-app/CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.

## Run / build

```bash
# Production API host (default)
flutter run -t lib/main.dart

# Local backend
flutter run \
  --dart-define=API_HOST=http://10.0.2.2:8000 \
  -t lib/main.dart

flutter build apk --release -t lib/main.dart
```

## Config chain

`API_HOST` dart-define → `lib/Env/env.dart` (`apiHost`) + login **Server** field → `TenantConfig` → `globals.baseUrl` (`{apiHost}/api/v1/{server}/`).

Use `TenantConfig.getServerName()` / `globals.tenantName` for runtime tenant; do not hardcode tenant slugs.

## Tenant settings

- Fetched **after login** via `SettingService.fetchPublicSettings()`
- Cached in SharedPreferences (`publicSettings`)
- Colors applied via `ColorConstants.applyFromPublicSettings()`
- On cold start: restore cached colors only (no settings API call)

Do not hardcode API URLs outside `env.dart` and `TenantConfig`. Entry point is `lib/main.dart` only.
